# Line endings are the same in every working copy, on every machine (4 Oct 2026).
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, and on the Windows PC that took over from the
# Mac, 457 of the 544 files came out with CRLF: the shell scripts (release.sh, repro.sh,
# zig-cc.sh) stop working under bash, and the texts the program embeds (include_str! of the
# panel's pages and of the i18n files) change, so a binary built there could never match the
# reproducible build. These rules win over core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept byte for byte as they are stored: published data (CSV with CRLF, as Excel expects it)
# and licence texts as their authors distribute them.
*.csv -text
OFL-*.txt -text

# Windows batch files need CRLF: cmd.exe misreads labels without it.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary, never converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.bmp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.msi binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.jks binary
*.exe binary
*.wasm binary
